    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0305" n="297" xml:id="pg297"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9791: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-30T16:00:00+08:00">August 30, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 30—11:04 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>563. Your [<hi rendition="#italic">Shanghai’s</hi>] 544, to the Department August
                    23, 10 p.m.;<anchor n="89" xml:id="d309-f1"/> also your [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shanghai’s</hi>] 548, August 24, 5 p.m. I have just received following
                    letter from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Referring to your letter addressed to the Minister for Foreign Affairs on
                        August 24th regarding the falling of air bombs in that part of the
                        International Settlement south of Soochow Creek on August 23d, I have the
                        honor to state that it is most regrettable that a number of persons were
                        killed or injured as a result of the incidents and that two American
                        citizens also received injuries. After a preliminary investigation by the
                        Chinese authorities concerned, it has been established that ever since the
                        opening of hostilities in Shanghai the Chinese Air Force has never used any
                        800-kilogram bombs.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Sent to Shanghai. Repeated to Department and Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
